  "term": "dwarfism",
  "definition": "Dwarfism is a marked reduction in body size within a population. In the source packet, it is described as a body-size shift often linked to isolation and to ecological or genetic pressures such as limited resources, extreme climates, founder effects, genetic drift, and local adaptation.",
